---
// Bellamente roadmap — the backlog, public. Loud about being early: v0.0.1 is usable, not complete.
import "../styles/machina.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Roadmap — Bellamente</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Where Bellamente is going. v0.0.1 is an early release — usable, local-first, and not at all complete." />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://bellamente.vercel.app/roadmap/" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Bellamente" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Roadmap - Bellamente" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Where Bellamente is going. v0.0.1 is usable, local-first, honest, and not complete." />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://bellamente.vercel.app/roadmap/" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="Roadmap - Bellamente" />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="Where Bellamente is going. v0.0.1 is usable, local-first, honest, and not complete." />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "WebPage",
      "name": "Roadmap - Bellamente",
      "description": "Where Bellamente is going. v0.0.1 is usable, local-first, honest, and not complete.",
      "url": "https://bellamente.vercel.app/roadmap/",
      "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "The Little AI Co" },
      "about": { "@type": "SoftwareApplication", "name": "Bellamente", "applicationCategory": "DeveloperApplication" }
    })}></script>    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wdth,wght@62..125,400..900&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;1,400&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <link
      rel="icon"
      href="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 32 32'%3E%3Ccircle cx='16' cy='16' r='6' fill='%23c4703a'/%3E%3Ccircle cx='16' cy='16' r='13' fill='none' stroke='%234fa487' stroke-opacity='.5' stroke-width='1.5'/%3E%3C/svg%3E"
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="db">
      <div class="wrap">
        <!-- section: nav -->
        <header class="db-nav">
          <a class="db-logo" href="/">Bella<span>mente</span></a>
          <nav aria-label="primary">
            <a href="/">Home</a>
            <a href="/docs">Docs</a>
            <a href="/changelog">Changelog</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/Jeff-Kazzee/bellamente">GitHub</a>
            <a class="cta" href="https://github.com/Jeff-Kazzee/bellamente/releases/download/v0.0.1/bella-windows-x64.exe">Download</a>
          </nav>
        </header>

        <!-- section: header + honesty banner -->
        <section class="db-hero">
          <p class="db-kicker">$ cat ROADMAP.md</p>
          <h1>Roadmap.
            <span class="thin">v0.0.1 is an early release. It is usable and it is honest — and it is not at all complete. This page is the actual backlog.</span>
          </h1>
          <div class="rm-banner" role="note">
            <b>Early software.</b> The memory core, the proxy, the traces, and the dashboard work today and
            are tested. Everything below is what's still missing. If a feature you need is on this list,
            it does not exist yet — no vaporware, no "coming soon" buttons that lie.
          </div>
          <div class="rm-banner" role="note">
            <b>Roadmaps move.</b> This sequence is a promise of direction, not a rigid queue: items can
            ship out of order, and multiple items may land together when one implementation clears several
            gaps. When that happens, shipped work moves from this page to the <a href="/changelog">changelog</a>.
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- section: shipped -->
        <section class="db-pillars">
          <div class="db-row">
            <span class="k">NOW · v0.0.1</span>
            <div>
              <h3>What works today</h3>
              <p>Memory lifecycle with versioned corrections and reversible forgetting · semantic +
                 hybrid document search · the drop-in proxy with memory grounding on buffered AND
                 streamed chats · auto-capture with local LLM distillation · full recall traces ·
                 the inspect dashboard · one binary, embedded Postgres+pgvector, local embeddings,
                 loopback by default.</p>
            </div>
            <div><span class="proof">116 behavior tests · coverage-gated builds</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="db-row">
            <span class="k">NEXT</span>
            <div>
              <h3>The trust loop, finished</h3>
              <p>Full-text search over memories (exact names and rare codes, not just semantic) ·
                 an MCP server (<span class="mono">bella mcp</span>) so agent tools plug in directly ·
                 recency-aware ranking · a retrieval eval harness with published numbers ·
                 richer trust views (why a capture was rejected, version diffs, provenance trees) ·
                 export/import so your memory is a file you can take anywhere.</p>
            </div>
            <div><span class="proof">in progress on the dev branch</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="db-row">
            <span class="k">LATER</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Memory-system parity</h3>
              <p>Time-aware facts (what was true when) · a review queue for inferred memories ·
                 smarter profiles with pinned facts · a context-window preview (see exactly what your
                 agent will see before it sees it) · a local folder-memory contract · reranking and
                 result diversity · usage analytics · scoped API keys.</p>
            </div>
            <div><span class="proof">specs first, then code</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="db-row">
            <span class="k">SOMEDAY</span>
            <div>
              <h3>The bigger bets</h3>
              <p>A memory graph you can see and export · an optional cross-encoder reranker ·
                 content extractors (PDF, code, web) · connectors (filesystem and Obsidian first) ·
                 SDKs and editor integrations · a desktop shell. Plugins over bloat — the core stays
                 one small binary.</p>
            </div>
            <div><span class="proof">plugin surfaces, not core</span></div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- section: principles -->
        <section class="db-proxy">
          <div>
            <h2>What will never change</h2>
            <p>Local-first by default. No telemetry. Every recall traceable. Every correction versioned.
               Forgetting reversible and audited. If a feature can't be made inspectable, it doesn't ship.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="db-flow" role="note" aria-label="Principles">
            <div class="hop">memory you can <b>inspect</b></div>
            <div class="hop">memory you can <b>correct</b></div>
            <div class="hop">memory that <b>never phones home</b></div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- section: footer -->
        <footer class="db-footer">
          <span>© 2026 The Little AI Co · BELLAMENTE</span>
          <span class="fine">
            follow progress or file an issue ·
            <a href="https://github.com/Jeff-Kazzee/bellamente">github.com/Jeff-Kazzee/bellamente</a>
          </span>
        </footer>
      </div>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>